# trail-hide.xrs - the sword's swing trail (VR-171): is it found on the player's
# pawn, does the native hide take, does it survive more attacks, and does the
# lever put it back?
#
# Needs: a loaded level in GAMEPLAY (look at an xrsim-shot first), [Mode]
# GamepadOnly=0. Run:  .\tools\xrsim-run.ps1 -Path .\tools\xrsim\trail-hide.xrs -Dir <sim dir>
#
# WHAT THIS CANNOT SAY. It asserts the MECHANICS: the component is found by its
# template, HiddenGame goes 0 -> 1 through the engine's own SetHidden, the engine
# does not show it again on the next attacks, and the lever shows and re-hides it.
# It does NOT assert that the ribbon is gone from the picture, because the ribbon
# could not be made to appear in a simulator capture at all: about 30 per-eye
# captures with the hide OFF, swept from 90 to 900 ms into an attack, with the hand
# still and with the hand sweeping through the view, never differed from idle by
# more than 0.2 % of pixels (the hilt moving). A capture A/B that cannot show the
# ribbon with the lever off cannot fail, so it is not here. The picture is the
# headset's to judge; F10 > Controls > Motion sword has the checkbox for the A/B.

hand r to grip 0.12 1.45 -0.45 0 0 0 800
@wait 1200
trigger r pull 300
@wait 2500

# 0. The path a player actually takes: the lever ON from launch and the trail not yet
#    created. It must be hidden as it appears AND still be held a moment later. The
#    first default-on run hid it and then lost it one scan later (a component 258 ms
#    old is not in the 2 s live-object table yet), after which the lever could not show
#    it again. `holding` is what catches that, so it is asserted after a wait.
@mod swordtrail on
@wait 500
trigger r pull 200
@wait 2500
@nolog trail: released component
@modassert features.swordTrail.holding eq 1

# 1. Lever off: an attack puts the trail on the pawn and nothing hides it.
@mod swordtrail off
@log trail: SHOWED component .* the lever went off
@modassert features.swordTrail.holding eq 0
@mark
trigger r pull 200
@wait 2000
@nolog trail: HID
@modassert features.swordTrail.hide eq false
@modassert features.swordTrail.trailsSeen ge 1
@modassert features.swordTrail.lastTemplate eq Sword_Trail
@modassert features.swordTrail.holding eq 0

# 2. Lever on: it is hidden where it sits, through the engine's own SetHidden.
@mark
@mod swordtrail on
@log trail: HID the sword trail .* via native SetHidden: HiddenGame 0 -> 1
@modassert features.swordTrail.holding eq 1

# 3. Three more attacks: the engine must not show it again behind our back. If it
#    did, the scan would hide it again and `hidden` would climb past 1 for this leg.
@mark
trigger r pull 200
@wait 2000
trigger r pull 200
@wait 2000
trigger r pull 200
@wait 2000
@nolog trail: HID
@nolog trail: SHOWED
@modassert features.swordTrail.holding eq 1
@modassert features.swordTrail.lastRefusal eq none

# 4. Lever off shows exactly the component we hid, and on hides it again.
@mark
@mod swordtrail off
@log trail: SHOWED component .* again \(hidden now 0\): the lever went off
@modassert features.swordTrail.holding eq 0
@mod swordtrail on
@log trail: HID the sword trail
@modassert features.swordTrail.holding eq 1

# 5. The census instrument still names what an attack adds (nothing new now: the
#    trail component is already attached, which is itself the finding).
@mark
@mod swordtrail census
@wait 500
trigger r pull 200
@log trail/census: done 8s
